<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nantes Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1434">1434</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> Cathedral, dedicated to Saints Peter and Paul, is the Gothic cathedral of Nantes in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, begun in 1434 under Duke John V of Brittany and completed only in 1891. It contains the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> tomb of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany and his wife Marguerite of Foix by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michel-colombe">Michel Colombe</a>. It was damaged by fire in 1972 and 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nantes-cathedral.jpg" alt="Nantes Cathedral" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eusebius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Pierre_de_Nantes_-_fa%C3%A7ade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
